{"name":"Lemon Cream","hex":"#fee193","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/250px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/500px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/250px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/250px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/500px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/250px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACitrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flowers_blossoms.jpg/500px-Flowers_blossoms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flowers_blossoms.jpg/960px-Flowers_blossoms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flowers_blossoms.jpg/500px-Flowers_blossoms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlowers_blossoms.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/P2101990%2Clemon.jpg/250px-P2101990%2Clemon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com